# Rewrites for blog.pixelmatch.art (Phase 1-2 deploy target).
#
# astro.config.mjs sets `base: '/blog'`, so:
#   - Internal hrefs and asset URLs emit with `/blog/` prefix
#   - canonical = https://pixelmatch.art/blog/...
# But CF Pages serves dist/* directly at the subdomain root. The
# rewrites below make `/blog/*` requests resolve to `dist/*`, so the
# Astro-emitted prefixed URLs work on the bare subdomain. Both
# `blog.pixelmatch.art/blog/learn/foo` and `blog.pixelmatch.art/learn/foo`
# resolve to the same content.
#
# Phase 3 (CF Worker on pixelmatch.art):
#   pixelmatch.art/blog/* → blog.pixelmatch.art/blog/*  (same path, no rewrite needed)
# Then we can drop the subdomain entirely from public-facing URLs;
# canonical was always pixelmatch.art/blog/... so Google sees no change.

/blog/_astro/*  /_astro/:splat  200
/blog/_pagefind/*  /_pagefind/:splat  200
/blog/sitemap.xml  /sitemap.xml  200
/blog/img/*  /img/:splat  200
/blog/*  /:splat  200
